# Sourced by build/build.sh (_setup_env.sh) as a build config, not merged as
# Kconfig, so this file is shell. It is what points the legacy build at our
# post-defconfig fragment; CONFIG_ lines here would only become shell variables.
#
# CONFIG_NTSYNC is forced to built-in after the merge: the backport's Kconfig
# entry is tristate and the tree's defconfig resolves it to =m, and 5.10/5.15
# never exported __vfs_setxattr_noperm, so the module link dies on
#
#   ERROR: modpost: "__vfs_setxattr_noperm" [drivers/misc/ntsync.ko] undefined!
#
# and the GKI module list then rejects the new entry:
#
#   +++ out/common/modules.order
#   +drivers/misc/ntsync.ko
#   ERROR: modules list out of date
#
# Built in, there is no .ko, so neither check has anything to complain about.
# The fragment entry alone is not enough: olddefconfig re-resolves a tristate
# back to the tree's default, so the value is re-forced first.
POST_DEFCONFIG_CMDS="( cd ${KERNEL_DIR} && scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m -O ${OUT_DIR} ${OUT_DIR}/.config ${ROOT_DIR}/common/wild_defconfig.fragment && scripts/config --file ${OUT_DIR}/.config --enable NTSYNC && make O=${OUT_DIR} ARCH=arm64 olddefconfig )"
